							<span class="text-zinc-600 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
						</summary>
						<p class="mt-4 text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
							The browser-first version is in active local preview. It is not being presented as a finished consumer release yet. The priority is to make the browser, Augmentor, Agent Control, Living Archive, provider routing, and add-on system work correctly before going wider.
						</p>
					</details>

					<!-- FAQ Item 3 -->
					<details class="bg-zinc-900/50 border border-zinc-800 rounded-lg p-6 hover:border-zinc-700 transition-colors group">
						<summary class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-100 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between">
							<span>What platforms will it run on?</span>
							<span class="text-zinc-600 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
						</summary>
						<p class="mt-4 text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
							The current build path is macOS-first while the browser host stabilizes. Windows and Linux remain part of the product target, but release readiness depends on deterministic browser, extension, provider, memory, and packaging validation.
						</p>
					</details>

					<!-- FAQ Item 4 -->
					<details class="bg-zinc-900/50 border border-zinc-800 rounded-lg p-6 hover:border-zinc-700 transition-colors group">
						<summary class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-100 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between">
							<span>Will this replace my current tools?</span>
							<span class="text-zinc-600 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
						</summary>
						<p class="mt-4 text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
							No. ResonantOS starts as the browser where AI can help you work. Add-ons can connect tools such as Hermes, OpenCode, Obsidian-style memory, and other workflows over time. The aim is augmentation, not replacement.
						</p>
					</details>

					<!-- FAQ Item 5 -->
					<details class="bg-zinc-900/50 border border-zinc-800 rounded-lg p-6 hover:border-zinc-700 transition-colors group">
						<summary class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-100 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between">
							<span>Can I build my own add-ons?</span>
							<span class="text-zinc-600 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
						</summary>
						<p class="mt-4 text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
							Yes — that is one of the core mandates. Add-ons can become alternative chat systems, memory systems, agent workspaces, browser tools, channels, or connectors. They run through explicit capability grants instead of unrestricted access. Structure over syntax.
						</p>
					</details>

					<!-- FAQ Item 6 -->
					<details class="bg-zinc-900/50 border border-zinc-800 rounded-lg p-6 hover:border-zinc-700 transition-colors group">
